 with horrible stories huge traumas  and serious tragedies citizen aggregated  area according to some estimates over  ten thousand women in Russia are killed  every year by injuries inflicted by a  partner but in many cases domestic  violence is not a criminal offense  extraneous key keeping screaming in  other countries there are mechanisms in  place to fight against domestic violence  on a state level restraining orders  strict legislation and law enforcement  agencies that are taught how to deal  with these situations unfortunately  Russia doesn't have that that's why more  cases here ended murder and more women  stay in abusive relationships because  they don't have the tools to get out of  them Valentina's hotel is located in  moscow zis mile of ski market before the  pandemic tourists bustle between stalls  of bric-a-brac and gaudy copies of  Russian style architecture valentina  hopes that paying guests will start  coming back soon she's nearly finished  renovating the rooms of her hotel a few  of them which Valentina is proud to show  off are done already but she also  doesn't want to stop taking in survivors  of domestic violence it's great we're  helping people and that gives everyone  at the hotel a good feeling even if it's  not always easy with the women and there  are sometimes tough situations knowing  that we are doing something good lifts  our spirits and makes us more ready to  fight for the hotel after the pandemic  Valentina's team plans to keep one or  two rooms available for the women the  hotel owner says in normal times that  shouldn't be a problem but the hotel's  shouldn't see this as a huge sacrifice  to society or is a huge expense it  actually costs almost nothing  essentially it's just the cost of  cleaning the sheets for many women  Valentina's commitment has already made  a  difference her time in the hotel has  given professional singer Anita the  strength to start over but it's not  summon a beast only a girl as merely my  much gave